          "section": "Must-fix",
          "position": 1,
          "key": "[P2; recovery/acceptance seam] `skills/super-code/scripts/dispatch-text.mjs:319` → `skills/super-code/coordinator.js:432–448` → `skills/super-auto/scripts/report-status:135–143`: immutable review-source metadata becomes an unsatisfiable measurement obligation after recovery. The producer writes `kind:\"deferred\"` with `data.reviewSource` only; the actual coordinator reader accepts and retains that record in `recoveryObligations`, which the returned Recovery snapshot and caller contract preserve. Acceptance handles every non-runFailure deferred record as a measurement, so this metadata lacks the required sourceTree/command/configuration. A read-only in-memory probe executed the actual captured reader and acceptance heredoc using the actual current binding from progress.md. With synthetic satisfied review/measurement/human controls and mocked clean projection/status, control returned exit 0, eligible:true; adding only the real binding returned exit 3, eligible:false, gap `review-source:inv-c96916a964634bb0bb5f2bd3b8e1769b: measurement identity unavailable`. This verifies deterministic classification, not actual run acceptance or a live resumed workflow. The first invocation may not reread its newly appended binding into memory; the supported resume/next-invocation path does. Preserve the immutable binding and distinguish it from actionable deferred measurement obligations; do not fabricate a test or delete binding history to pass acceptance. Add a focused producer→recovery→acceptance control with real binding metadata and independently satisfied actual acceptance prerequisites. Full probe, raw outputs, and exact source hashes are retained in the companion package.",
          "text": "[P2; recovery/acceptance seam] `skills/super-code/scripts/dispatch-text.mjs:319` → `skills/super-code/coordinator.js:432–448` → `skills/super-auto/scripts/report-status:135–143`: immutable review-source metadata becomes an unsatisfiable measurement obligation after recovery. The producer writes `kind:\"deferred\"` with `data.reviewSource` only; the actual coordinator reader accepts and retains that record in `recoveryObligations`, which the returned Recovery snapshot and caller contract preserve. Acceptance handles every non-runFailure deferred record as a measurement, so this metadata lacks the required sourceTree/command/configuration. A read-only in-memory probe executed the actual captured reader and acceptance heredoc using the actual current binding from progress.md. With synthetic satisfied review/measurement/human controls and mocked clean projection/status, control returned exit 0, eligible:true; adding only the real binding returned exit 3, eligible:false, gap `review-source:inv-c96916a964634bb0bb5f2bd3b8e1769b: measurement identity unavailable`. This verifies deterministic classification, not actual run acceptance or a live resumed workflow. The first invocation may not reread its newly appended binding into memory; the supported resume/next-invocation path does. Preserve the immutable binding and distinguish it from actionable deferred measurement obligations; do not fabricate a test or delete binding history to pass acceptance. Add a focused producer→recovery→acceptance control with real binding metadata and independently satisfied actual acceptance prerequisites. Full probe, raw outputs, and exact source hashes are retained in the companion package."
        }
