    {
      "ref": {
        "source": "inv-mvc60k41-xt8p35rk04d/task-14-review",
        "section": "Findings — adapter/review-finding/raw-section-5/raw-byte-000001114",
        "position": 1
      },
      "occurrences": [
        {
          "source": "inv-mvc60k41-xt8p35rk04d/task-14-review",
          "artifact": "legacy-report-adapters-r1/19-task-14-review.md",
          "section": "Findings — adapter/review-finding/raw-section-5/raw-byte-000001114",
          "position": 1,
          "key": "skills/super-auto/scripts/report-status:107 — Discover and archive the actual direct-review package `final-review-ID.md.diff`. The collector discovers only `prefix+'.diff'`, while the real Workflow producer at skills/super-code/coordinator.js:2757 invokes review-package with `${reviewPath}.diff` and reviewPath is `final-review-ID.md`. A settled direct review can therefore return collection complete without preserving its input diff, allowing cleanup to destroy that source. The same incorrect suffix in hasBundle (:93) can classify a null/no-work return with a leftover actual direct package as artifact-free. Update discovery and null bundle detection to match the producer, and use producer-shaped .md.diff fixtures (tests/super-auto/test-scripts.sh:352 currently invents the shorter .diff filename). Retain byte-for-byte/idempotent archive assertions for that real filename.",
