          "key": "[Blocking] skills/super-code/coordinator.js:25",
          "text": "[Blocking] skills/super-code/coordinator.js:25 — Omitting the supported invocationId makes Workflow startup call forbidden Date.now() and Math.random() APIs and abort before logging or dispatch. [lanes: concurrency-async]\n  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute ✗-survived / ground ✓)\n  evidence: The documented contract says the script mints an ID when omitted; official Claude Code Workflow documentation says these clock/random APIs throw inside a script. Frozen-source VM checks show base starts without an ID and head throws before its first log; an explicit ID is a positive control. The documented dryRun examples do include invocationId, correcting the original evidence's contrary claim; the omission path remains explicitly supported. Evidence: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/workflows; docs/superpowers/runs/2026-10-16-workflow-reliability/2026-10-16-workflow-reliability-roast-pr-1-stages/judge-1-ground/repro.mjs and docs/superpowers/runs/2026-10-16-workflow-reliability/2026-10-16-workflow-reliability-roast-pr-1-stages/judge-1-ground/repro-runtime-result.json.\n  fix-shape hint: Mint the identifier outside the deterministic Workflow script and pass it through args."
        }
